 pawns can't block on f8, and they can't move to h6 or h5 from h7 either. So, while pawns can move, any attempt won't help in blocking the check.**Verifying checkmate scenarios**\n\nI've confirmed that during check, any legal move that puts the king out of check is valid, but a move like g7 to g6 doesn't work as it doesn't block the check. So, only the king can move or capture pieces, which leads to checkmate. \n\nI'm then outlining a scenario for a smothered mate using a knight. The setup includes checking that the king on h8 is effectively trapped by its own pieces. After verifying the FEN for the positions and moves, I ensure no other pawn movements will change the check status. This thorough checking affirms that the proposed moves lead to a successful checkmate scenario.",
